          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.305,
            0.848,
            0.345
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "11. Find out how many coins should be stacked to match the height of the Statue of Unity. Assume each coin is 1 mm thick."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.349,
            0.848,
            0.443
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "12. Grey-headed albatrosses have a roughly 7-feet wide wingspan. They are known to migrate across several oceans. Albatrosses can cover about 900 – 1000 km in a day. One of the longest single trips recorded is about 12,000 km. How many days would such a trip take to cross the Pacific Ocean approximately?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.446,
            0.849,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13. A bar-tailed godwit holds the record for the longest recorded non-stop flight. It travelled 13,560 km from Alaska to Australia without stopping. Its journey started on 13 October 2022 and continued for about 11 days. Find out the approximate distance it covered every day. Find out the approximate distance it covered every hour."
            }
          ]
        },
